@q 36:4

The **cell** was first seen by **Robert Hooke** (1665, cork); the **cell theory** is due to **Schleiden and Schwann** (1838-39). The **nucleus** controls heredity and cell reproduction, so statement (b) is false.

@section 21.2 | Heredity and DNA

@q 37:1-4

**Gregor Mendel** (father of genetics) crossed **garden peas** (*Pisum sativum*) and found the laws of **dominance, segregation and independent assortment** (1866). A **gene** is a functional segment of DNA and the unit of heredity; a change in its base sequence is a **mutation**. **Genome mapping** locates genes on chromosomes; the **Human Genome Project** was completed in 2003 (about 20,000 genes), and India's **Genome India** project sequenced 10,000 Indians (data released 2025).

@q 37:5-7

@table
Feature | DNA | RNA
Sugar | **Deoxyribose** | Ribose
Bases | **Adenine, guanine, cytosine, thymine** | A, G, C, **uracil**
Strands | **Double helix** (Watson and Crick, 1953, using Rosalind Franklin's X-ray data) | Usually single
Job | Stores genetic information | Carries the code and makes proteins
@end

**Tyrosine** is an amino acid, not a DNA base. **Har Gobind Khorana** helped crack the genetic code (Nobel 1968), and **Jacob and Monod** explained gene regulation (the lac operon).

@q 37:8-9

Humans have **46 chromosomes** (23 pairs: 22 pairs of autosomes + XX or XY). Sex is fixed by the father's sperm (X or Y). Many **reptiles** (most turtles, crocodiles and some lizards) have no sex chromosomes; the **incubation temperature** of the eggs decides their sex.

@section 21.3 | Biofertilizers

@q 38:1

**Biofertilizers** are cultures of living micro-organisms that add nutrients to soil by fixing nitrogen or dissolving phosphate. They are cheap and eco-friendly.

@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 2001, 2002
Which of the following is/are used as biofertilizers?
1. Azolla
2. Blue-green algae
3. Alfalfa
4. Nitrolin
Select the correct answer from the codes given below:
Codes :
(a) 2 and 4
(b) 1, 2 and 4
(c) 2, 3 and 4
(d) 1, 2 and 3
@ans (*)
@note **Azolla** and **blue-green algae** are biofertilizers; **alfalfa** is a legume crop (a green manure), and **Nitrolin** is a chemical (calcium cyanamide) fertiliser. No option has only 1 and 2, so the source marks the question (*).
@end
